60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Plan B is impossible. The late-turn pool is already exhausted; we cannot extend hours without a massive recruitment drive.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Plan D is exactly what the pilot eight years ago proved was possible. It's a proven win.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Plan C is a trap. The pre-war shells will lead to endless delays and cost overruns. Plan D's ferry integration is a bureaucratic nightmare.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Plan D... it replaces the contractors. If we can stop paying those separate fees, we might actually save money.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Plan A! The mid-city runs are taking way too long, and the boarding islands will help the connection times!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, Plan A requires more drivers. Do we have them? I suspect we don't.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, the ""nightmare"" is just paperwork. The technical side is already solved. Plan D is the safest bet.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, paperwork is where these projects die. However, Plan A avoids the shells and the night-shift crisis.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Plan D is the only one that addresses the budget leak. I'm... I'm leaning toward that.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,But Plan A fixes the actual time loss! Why are we talking about paperwork when people are waiting for buses?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I cannot support B. I can support A if the drivers are outsourced, but D is the most stable for the current crew.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,Plan D is the only one that isn't just guessing. It's based on a successful pilot. I'm sticking with it.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Plan A is the most physically viable. Plan D's reliance on the ferry operators' agreement is a significant risk.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want to argue, but the contractor fees are just too high. Plan D seems... right.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,No way! Plan A is the only one that actually helps the passengers get home faster! Let's go with A!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I will vote for D. It is the only option that doesn't place an impossible burden on our exhausted staff.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting D. We have the data from eight years ago. Let's actually use it for once.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for A. It avoids the structural risks of C and the administrative deadlock of D.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'll vote for D too. I think it's the only way to fix the budget.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"Aww, you're all boring! I'm voting for A because it's the only one that fixes the real problem!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
